      "feedback": "The graph’s equilibrium is $12 and 200 thousand workers, above the $6 minimum. At $6, Qd = 300 thousand and Qs = 100 thousand: a shortage of 200 thousand. A ceiling could hold wages there, but a floor permits the equilibrium wage.",
