      "id": "ERQ-P52A-OPPC-B3-001",
      "q": "A city assigns its only crew and an $8 million project budget to a rail extension that uses all 12 available crew-weeks. Alternative projects are indivisible and can be sequenced; their resource use and net benefits add. Water repairs need 12 weeks and $8 million, with $24 million net benefit. Drainage needs 5 weeks and $3 million, with $14 million net benefit. Bridge work needs 7 weeks and $5 million, with $15 million net benefit. A hospital upgrade needs 6 weeks and $5 million, with $20 million net benefit. All net benefits already deduct project spending. What is the best feasible alternative forgone by selecting rail?",
