      "commonError": "confuses_income_change_with_movement_along_demand",
      "feedback": "Income raises normal-good demand. A cheaper substitute and a dearer complement reduce it. Observed growth is the net result and cannot identify the isolated income effect; a fixed own price does not prevent a demand shift.",
